## [upstream] specfunc: improve the accuracy of lambert_W0 for small arguments

Commit: fb2b4e4cd

`gsl_sf_lambert_W0_e(x)` always used the Halley iteration, whose `w -= t`
step cancels catastrophically for `x` near zero; the relative error grew as
`x` decreased and below about `1e-50` the result collapsed to zero.  For
`|x| < 1e-3 * GSL_DBL_EPSILON` it now returns `x`, and for `|x| < 1e-5` it
evaluates the Taylor series (Fukushima 2013).  The relative error is now of
order machine epsilon across the range.

Files: `specfunc/lambert.c`, plus tests in `specfunc/test_sf.c`.

See Savannah bug #60741.


