## [upstream] randist: handle the degenerate mu = 0 in gsl_ran_poisson_pdf

Commit: 4f9f4f4fc

`gsl_ran_poisson_pdf()` evaluated `exp (log (mu) * k - lf - mu)`, so with
`mu = 0` and `k = 0` the term `log (mu) * k` is `-inf * 0` and the result
was `NaN`.  A Poisson distribution of rate zero is the degenerate one and
carries all of its mass at `k = 0`, so `mu = 0` is now special cased and
returns 1 for `k = 0` and 0 otherwise.

The patch in the bug report also adds a guard to `gsl_ran_poisson()`.
That half is not applied: the Knuth loop in the sampler already returns
`k = 0` for `mu = 0`, so the guard would be dead code.

File: `randist/poisson.c`.

See Savannah bug #43326.


## [upstream] linalg: increase the cholesky_invert Hilbert test tolerance

Commit: f84a57a0f

The unscaled 4x4 Hilbert matrix is nearly singular, and the residual
accuracy of `gsl_linalg_cholesky_invert` depends on the order in which
CBLAS accumulates `dsymm`, which in turn changes when the compiler
auto-vectorises the loop.  The multiplier of 256 was exceeded by about
12% on builds enabling AVX-512, and the same can happen with aarch64
NEON.  It is raised to 512, which is what `gsl_linalg_mcholesky_invert`
already uses for the same test; `gsl_linalg_pcholesky_invert` uses 1024.

Only a test tolerance changes here, the library is unaffected.

File: `linalg/test_cholesky.c`.

See Savannah bug #67445.


