## [upstream] linalg: define the LU pivot array before building the permutation

Commit: d73ba5300

`gsl_linalg_LU_decomp()` and `gsl_linalg_complex_LU_decomp()` allocate
`ipiv` and call `LU_decomp_L3()`, which for `N > 24` recurses on
sub-blocks.  When a singular pivot is met in the leading sub-block the
recursion returns immediately without writing the tail of `ipiv`, and the
caller then reads the whole array to build the permutation.  That produced
a permutation built from uninitialised memory, and `p->data[pivi]` could
index outside the permutation.  `LU_decomp_L2()`, used for `N <= 24`,
already wrote every entry even when singular, so the defect only showed on
larger matrices.

`ipiv` is now initialized to the identity immediately after allocation, in
both functions.  `LU_decomp_L3()` recurses on views of that same buffer, so
every entry is defined before any read; entries the factorization does not
reach stay no-ops, which is the correct "no interchange" placeholder.  This
is preferable to the submitted `if (!status)` guard, which also discarded
